            %em Geometric quantization via push-forward
            or
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^{\mathbb{C}}
              \-quantization
            is a variant of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            in which the step from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundle"} prequantum bundle
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states"} space of states
            is not (explicitly) performed by a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            and forming the space of polarized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            and forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+differential+K-theory"} fiber integration in differential K-theory
            of the prequantum connection. Specifically, this refines the notion of geometric quantization via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarizations"} Kähler polarizations
