                    in
                    %a{:href => "Diaconescu-Moore-Witten+anomaly#ReferencesInterpretationInSecondMoravaKTheory"} Kriz-Sati interpretation
          %h2#References References
          %p A survey is in
          %ul
            %li
              Reyer Sjamaar,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic reduction and Riemann-Roch formulas for multiplicities
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1996-33-03/S0273-0979-96-00661-1/"} AMS
          %p The idea originates around
          %ul#Metzler
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Metzler"}> David Metzler
              ,
              %em A K-Theoretic Note on Geometric Quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9809031"}> arXiv:math/9809031
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Duistermaat"}> Hans Duistermaat
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"} Victor Guillemin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckhard+Meinrenken"} Eckhard Meinrenken
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Siye+Wu"} Siye Wu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic reduction and Riemann-Roch for circle actions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://intlpress.com/_newsite/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/mrl/1995/0002/0003/MRL-1995-0002-0003-A-003.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and is highlighted in the general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Viktor+Ginzburg"}> Viktor Ginzburg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"} Victor Guillemin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yael+Karshon"} Yael Karshon
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Moment maps, cobordisms, and Hamiltonian group actions
              %p (Section 6.8 “Geometric quantization as a push-forward”)
          %p and the last section of
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                Stable complex and
                = succeed "-structures" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Spin
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StableComplexSpinC.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A detailed analysis of push-forward quantization of general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+manifolds"} presymplectic manifolds
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ana+Canas+da+Silva"}> Ana Canas da Silva
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yael+Karshon"} Yael Karshon
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Presymplectic Manifolds and Circle Actions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9705008"} arXiv:dg-ga/9705008
          %p
            A first proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillemin-Sternberg+geometric+quantization+conjecture"} Guillemin-Sternberg geometric quantization conjecture
            in terms of
            = succeed "-quantization" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckhard+Meinrenken"}> Eckhard Meinrenken
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Symplectic surgery and the
                  = succeed "-Dirac" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
          %p
            A suggestion that geometric push-forward quantization is best understood to proceed to take values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            is in
          %ul#Bos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Functorial quantization and the Guillemin-Sternberg conjecture
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0307059"} arXiv:math-ph/0307059
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rogier+Bos"}> Rogier Bos
                ,
                %em Groupoids in geometric quantization
                PhD Thesis (2007) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ist.utl.pt/~rbos/ProefschriftA4.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            A refined realization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillemin-Sternberg+geometric+quantization+conjecture"} Guillemin-Sternberg geometric quantization conjecture
            was conjectured in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Hochs"}> Peter Hochs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              %em The Guillemin-Sternberg conjecture for noncompact groups and spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0512022"}> arXiv:math-ph/0512022
              )
          %p based on the thesis
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Hochs"}> Peter Hochs
              ,
              %em Quantisation commutes with reduction for cocompact Hamiltonian group actions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ru.nl/~landsman/ThesisPeterHochs.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and was proven in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"}> Varghese Mathai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weiping+Zhang"} Weiping Zhang
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization for proper actions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0806.3138"} arXiv:0806.3138
          %p Similar discussion is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Emile+Paradan"}> Paul-Emile Paradan
              ,
              %em Spin-quantization commutes with reduction
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.1067"}> arXiv:0911.1067
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Emile+Paradan"}> Paul-Emile Paradan
              ,
              %em Localization of the Riemann-Roch character
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9911024"}> arXiv:math/9911024
              )
          %p
            Discussion of push-forward not over manifolds but over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            as relevant in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FreedHopkinsTeleman07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
                %em Consistent Orientation of Moduli Spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1909"}> arXiv:0711.1909
                ), chapter XIX, pages 395-419 in: Oscar Garcia-Prada, Jean Pierre Bourguignon,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Salamon"} Simon Salamon
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Many Facets of Geometry: A Tribute to Nigel Hitchin
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.oxfordscholarship.com/view/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199534920.001.0001/acprof-9780199534920"} doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199534920.001.0001
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shay+Fuchs"}> Shay Fuchs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi ℂ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^{\mathbb{C}}
                    \-quantization, prequantization and cutting
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://tspace.library.utoronto.ca/bitstream/1807/11205/1/Fuchs_Shay_Z_200806_PhD_thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of this push-forward quantization as higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local prequantum boundary field theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/thesisNuiten.pdf"} thesis pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://dspace.library.uu.nl/handle/1874/282756"} archived version
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/thesisNuitenTalk.pdf"} talk slides
        .revisedby
